IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `maia-dates`
IMPORT `maia-claims`

-- Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in maia-claims.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the date`

-- The accident: 1 March 2024. 3 months after: 1 June 2024 (day 92). 28 days after: 29 March 2024. 3 years after:
-- 1 March 2027 (day 1095).
`A` MEANS `d` 1 3 2024

`first notice` MEANS `the notice about the first 52 weeks after the accident`
`later notice` MEANS `the notice about the time after the first 52 weeks`
`s 3.14` MEANS `a medical certificate, or an authority for my treatment providers to give it information (s 3.14)`
`s 3.15` MEANS `a certificate of fitness for work, or a declaration about work (s 3.15)`

§§ `s 6.13(1) -- by when`

#ASSERT `By when must I claim statutory benefits` `A` EQUALS `d` 1 6 2024
-- Month ends: 30 November plus 3 months is the last day of February (29 in 2024, 28 in 2025); 31 December -> 31 March.
#ASSERT `By when must I claim statutory benefits` (`d` 30 11 2023) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `By when must I claim statutory benefits` (`d` 30 11 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I claim statutory benefits` (`d` 31 12 2024) EQUALS `d` 31 3 2025

§§ `s 6.13(2) -- the 28-day step`

#ASSERT `By when must I claim to be paid weekly payments from the start` `A` EQUALS `d` 29 3 2024
-- Across 29 February 2024: 20 February plus 28 days is 19 March.
#ASSERT `By when must I claim to be paid weekly payments from the start` (`d` 20 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 19 3 2024
-- Arguments: accident; claim day; a full and satisfactory explanation for the late claim (Regulation cl 8A).
#ASSERT `Are weekly payments payable for the time before my claim` `A` (`d` 29 3 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are weekly payments payable for the time before my claim` `A` (`d` 30 3 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are weekly payments payable for the time before my claim` `A` (`d` 30 3 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- cl 8A(1)(a): within 3 months -- 1 June 2024 yes, 2 June 2024 no.
#ASSERT `Are weekly payments payable for the time before my claim` `A` (`d` 1 6 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are weekly payments payable for the time before my claim` `A` (`d` 2 6 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- cl 8A(4): an accident on 1 March 2023 (before 1 April 2023), no; on 1 April 2023, yes (claim 30 April 2023, day 29).
#ASSERT `Are weekly payments payable for the time before my claim` (`d` 1 3 2023) (`d` 30 3 2023) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are weekly payments payable for the time before my claim` (`d` 1 4 2023) (`d` 30 4 2023) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 6.13(1), (3), (4) -- is my claim in time (the MUST rule and its late-claim LEST)`

-- Arguments: accident; claim day; explanation; death or over 10%; treatment-and-care-only after workers compensation
-- medical stopped; the day it stopped.
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` `A` FALSE FALSE FALSE `A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 1 6 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE `A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 2 6 2024) FALSE FALSE FALSE `A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 2 6 2024) TRUE FALSE FALSE `A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The 3 years: the last day 1 March 2027 yes; 2 March 2027 no; with a death or over 10%, no outer limit.
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE FALSE FALSE `A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 2 3 2027) TRUE FALSE FALSE `A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 2 3 2027) TRUE TRUE FALSE `A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 2 3 2030) TRUE TRUE FALSE `A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 2 3 2027) FALSE TRUE FALSE `A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 6.13(4): workers compensation medical expenses stopped 1 January 2030; 3 months: to 1 April 2030.
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 1 4 2030) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 2 4 2030) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 1 1 2030) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim for statutory benefits in time` `A` (`d` 1 12 2029) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 6.19 -- the insurer's notice on liability`

-- Claim on 10 March 2024: the 4 weeks end on 7 April 2024; the 9 months on 10 December 2024.
#ASSERT `By when must my insurer tell me whether it accepts liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `first notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`d` 7 4 2024)
#ASSERT `By when must my insurer tell me whether it accepts liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `later notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`d` 10 12 2024)
#ASSERT `By when must my insurer tell me whether it accepts liability` (`d` 31 5 2024) `later notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`d` 28 2 2025)
#ASSERT `By when must my insurer tell me whether it accepts liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `first notice` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: claim day; which notice; notice given; the day given; the day asked about; 2022 amendments apply.
#ASSERT `Is my insurer taken to have accepted liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `first notice` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 7 4 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my insurer taken to have accepted liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `first notice` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 8 4 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my insurer taken to have accepted liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `first notice` TRUE (`d` 7 4 2024) (`d` 1 5 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my insurer taken to have accepted liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `first notice` TRUE (`d` 8 4 2024) (`d` 1 5 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my insurer taken to have accepted liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `first notice` TRUE (`d` 8 4 2024) (`d` 7 4 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my insurer taken to have accepted liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `first notice` TRUE (`d` 20 3 2024) (`d` 20 3 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my insurer taken to have accepted liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `later notice` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 10 12 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my insurer taken to have accepted liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `later notice` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 11 12 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my insurer taken to have accepted liability` (`d` 10 3 2024) `first notice` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 8 4 2024) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 3.14, 3.15 -- the insurer's requirements`

#ASSERT `By when must I give my insurer what it asked for` `s 3.14` (`d` 1 5 2024) EQUALS `d` 15 5 2024
#ASSERT `By when must I give my insurer what it asked for` `s 3.15` (`d` 1 5 2024) EQUALS `d` 8 5 2024

-- Arguments: requirement; the day told; complied; the day complied; the day asked about.
#ASSERT `Can my insurer suspend my weekly payments for this` `s 3.14` (`d` 1 5 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 15 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my insurer suspend my weekly payments for this` `s 3.14` (`d` 1 5 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 16 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my insurer suspend my weekly payments for this` `s 3.14` (`d` 1 5 2024) TRUE (`d` 15 5 2024) (`d` 20 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Complied late (18 May): the failure no longer continues on 20 May.
#ASSERT `Can my insurer suspend my weekly payments for this` `s 3.14` (`d` 1 5 2024) TRUE (`d` 18 5 2024) (`d` 20 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Will comply on 25 May: on 20 May the failure continues.
#ASSERT `Can my insurer suspend my weekly payments for this` `s 3.14` (`d` 1 5 2024) TRUE (`d` 25 5 2024) (`d` 20 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my insurer suspend my weekly payments for this` `s 3.15` (`d` 1 5 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 8 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my insurer suspend my weekly payments for this` `s 3.15` (`d` 1 5 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 9 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 3.15 -- certificate of fitness`

-- Arguments: first day covered; last day covered; special reasons accepted; day provided; the day asked about.
-- 1-28 May is 28 days: day 28 covered.
#ASSERT `Does my certificate of fitness count for this day` (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 28 5 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 28 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 1-29 May is 29 days: the 29th day NOTHING without special reasons, yes with them; day 28 still yes.
#ASSERT `Does my certificate of fitness count for this day` (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 29 5 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 29 5 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does my certificate of fitness count for this day` (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 29 5 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 28 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my certificate of fitness count for this day` (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 29 5 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 29 5 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my certificate of fitness count for this day` (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 28 5 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 30 4 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my certificate of fitness count for this day` (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 28 5 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2024) (`d` 29 5 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3.15(5): provided 31 March 2024; 1 January 2024 is 90 days before (yes); 31 December 2023 is 91 days before (no).
#ASSERT `Does my certificate of fitness count for this day` (`d` 1 1 2024) (`d` 28 1 2024) FALSE (`d` 31 3 2024) (`d` 1 1 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my certificate of fitness count for this day` (`d` 31 12 2023) (`d` 27 1 2024) FALSE (`d` 31 3 2024) (`d` 31 12 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 6.14 -- claim for damages`

#ASSERT `By when must I claim damages` `A` EQUALS `d` 1 3 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I claim damages` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
-- Arguments: accident; claim day; explanation.
#ASSERT `Can I make my claim for damages` `A` (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I make my claim for damages` `A` (`d` 2 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I make my claim for damages` `A` (`d` 2 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
